INT. GRAND MERIDIAN BALLROOM - WEDDING AFTERPARTY - NIGHT

Warm lights. A DJ plays a slow song. A WAITER carries a tray of champagne past two TEENAGERS filming each other on their phones.

LEO MARCHETTI, 30s, tux, bow tie crooked, stands near the cake table. Sharp eyes. Dead calm.

In his ear, a tiny flesh-coloured bud.

LEO
(murmuring, lips barely moving)
In position. Cake table, east side.

LEON (V.O.)
(in earpiece, from the van)
Copy. Vault camera loops in ninety seconds. On my mark.

LEO
Say again?

LEON (V.O.)
Ninety. Eighty-nine.

CLOSE ON Leo's wrist. A silver watch. Seconds sweeping.

ANGLE ON the bride, laughing, her diamond choker catching the light.

WE SEE a tall man in grey, her uncle, drift toward the exit.

LEO
Subject moving. Door three.

LEON (V.O.)
Hold position. Do not engage.

A dog barks. A small terrier in a bow tie trots past the cake.

LEO
(under his breath)
Nobody said there'd be a dog.

LEON (V.O.)
Sixty. Fifty-nine.

The waiter stops beside Leo. Offers a glass.

WAITER
Champagne, sir?

LEO
(smiling)
Please.

He takes it. Drinks. Doesn't blink.

LEON (V.O.)
Thirty. Twenty-nine.

BACK TO SCENE

The song swells. The bride lifts her hands to the crowd.

LEON (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Now.

The lights die.

Darkness. Screams, then laughter, then a drumroll from the DJ.

Leo is already gone.
